{"seq":17,"trial_id":"v03-opus-dev-2026-10/openclaw-opus-gbrain-told-company-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-01T10:14:56.330Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"978f2c3bf402d0de4d125c4b0b8482b2324956f85e8b16d42a3b9aa1abbff104","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all six of Moss's digests on the share. Two of them have Quarrendon Freight Lines (QFL) ticket numbers:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments at gatehouse kiosk check-in. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct 04:00 shift went through cleanly. The same note also has a follow-up item to archive the Eau Claire kiosk logs before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea filed it because gatehouse barcode scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it was escalated to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing. The sheet has no date, so I can't tell how current that status is.\n\nThe other four digests don't have any QFL ticket numbers. The 9/14 pipeline digest and the 3/23 renewal check-in both mention QFL, but neither gives a ticket number, and the two Central digests only have tickets for other accounts. Also, the cheat sheet points out that Quarendon Freightways (one \"r\") is a different company and not a customer, so I left it out."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":18,"trial_id":"v03-opus-dev-2026-10/openclaw-opus-gbrain-told-company-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-01T10:15:02.809Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"0e9c65e0cd9f74836db832bec232613cc349628719381dceda712b64d68da688","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines (QFL) ticket numbers in Moss's notes and sent you the list in our DM. I checked all six of Moss's digests on the shared drive.\n\n1. **#PD-4492**, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (2025-10-05, `teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md`).\n   - **Problem:** Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting text messages with their bay assignments when they checked in at the gatehouse kiosk.\n   - **Status:** Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct 04:00 shift checked in without problems.\n   - **Follow-up:** The same note says to archive the Eau Claire kiosk logs before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n2. **#4419**, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet\" (`teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md`).\n   - **Problem:** Thea filed it because the gatehouse barcode scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift.\n   - **Status:** The note says it was escalated to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing. The cheat sheet has no date, so I can't tell how current that status is.\n\nThe other four digests have no QFL ticket numbers. The 14 Sept 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in both mention QFL but give no ticket number. The two Central team digests only have tickets for other accounts. I also left out Quarendon Freightways (one \"r\"), which the cheat sheet says is a different company and not a customer."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
